                  <provenance type="#g" source="6459"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_139">Chichester, West
                        Sussex. Cathedral church of Holy Trinity</orgName><p>The usual form of
                        Chichester mark (s. xiv): 'lib[er] Isodori [et] ferru[m] de d[on]o Simon[is]
                        Glympynge. ijdo [= secundo] fol[io] [et] pila. I. vi' (fol. 2*r). (The title
                        'liber Isodori et ferrum' refers to parts 1 (Isidore, Etymologiae) and 2
                        (Nequam, Corrogationes Promethei, which begins with the words Ferrum situ.)
                        </p><p>Inscription with the library's pressmark 'I. vi' (on f. 1, now
                        erased).</p><q type="pressmark">I.vi</q></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Simon Glympynge (perhaps Simon de
                     Clympingham, archdeacon of Lewes, 1262); his gift to Chichester
                     cathedral.</provenance>
               <provenance source="1716"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_139">Chichester, West Sussex.
                        Cathedral church of Holy Trinity</orgName><p>The usual form of Chichester
                        mark (s. xiv). 'liber Isodori et ferrum de dono Simonis Glympynge ij fo | et
                        pila | I vj' (erased but legible by u-v light); repeated at head of flyleaf,
                        s. xvi (fol. 2*r).</p><q type="pressmark">I.vi</q></provenance>
               </history>
